  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% benchmark and the 55 °C test, but a model that exceeds the limit can keep being placed on the market while a corrective-action plan runs (up to 24 months for existing models), so the sales stop is effectively removed; this favours Northwind's Hearth 10. The S5 recall trigger is a mandatory 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while per-model results go to customers and regulators but not to the general public, which both red lines accommodated. S3 gives a six-year retrofit window, and S4 requires built-in suppression within 36 months."
